00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:12.650
<i>My levels when I made close contact 
with Kanade-chan are higher.</i>

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:15.450
<i>These mean...</i>

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:17.600
Himuro-senpai.

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:21.850
Unfortunately, those results are indisputable.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:27.300
<i>So we really don't love each other. 
Is that what this means?</i>

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:28.610
Wait.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.990
It's too soon to come to a conclusion.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:31.970
Yukimura-kun?

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:35.750
True, our oxytocin levels are low.

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:37.990
I'd say that's a reasonable result.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.000
Huh?

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.440
Interesting.

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:48.140
If you base it on Helen Fisher and 
others' "Three-year Romance Theory"!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:54.000
Science Fell in Love,
So I Tried to Prove It [<b>r=1-sinθ</b>]

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:58.720
<i><b>Usachuu</b></i>

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:58.720
<i><b>Princess Lychee</b></i>

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:58.720
Take that! You...

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.980
You little... You can't be serious!

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:05.090
It's your fault for not being 
able to land the finishing blow.

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:08.610
At this rate, fighting the CPU 
would make for better training.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.890
I'm never battling you again!

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:14.750
Losing then running is the 
greatest strength of the weak.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.350
Hmph!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.920
Helen Fisher?

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:22.880
Three-year Romance Theory?

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:27.200
What do you mean by a 
"reasonable result," Yukimura-kun?

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.740
May I ask for an explanation?

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:32.270
They say that there are 
two stages to romance.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:37.000
One of them is a state of great, 
burning passion—the romance phase.

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.670
When a person falls in love,

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:43.910
they first experience violent 
emotions in the romance phase.

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:47.410
<i>My heart is pounding.</i>

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.390
<i>I love him more than anything else!</i>

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.320
<i>Whether I'm asleep or awake, 
I keep thinking of him.</i>

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:58.160
<i>When I think that he might grow to 
hate me, it makes me so scared!</i>

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:00.860
<i>Now that he mentions it...</i>

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:03.500
<i>Little things making you happy...</i>

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:04.640
<i>or angry.</i>

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:07.310
<i>Having daydreams about 
the two of you together.</i>

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:11.890
<i>While we were traveling, I wanted to 
snuggle so badly I couldn't stand it.</i>

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:11.890
<i>Kiss! Kiss! Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!</i>

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:15.320
<i>Then he'd be so dense, 
it made me want to knee him.</i>

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:18.710
Unstable positive and negative emotions...

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:21.540
Are those romantic emotions?

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.200
At such moments,

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:26.120
within the brain, 
the pleasure hormone, dopamine,

