Some of you idiot humans with keen intuition 
may already have noticed, bear,

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:02.660
basically, we're talking 
about adrenaline here, bear.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:06.480
For some reason, in America 
they call it norepinephrine.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:15.850
<b>Adrenaline = Norepinephrine</b>

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:07.310
Huh?

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:10.430
"It's hard to understand, 
so just call it adrenaline," bear?

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:15.850
Calling it "norepinephrine" is more 
specialized, so it sounds cooler, bear!

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:18.350
In the brain...?

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:20.710
Addiction?

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.740
In short, it means this!

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:27.530
<i>My heart is pounding!</i>

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.420
<i>I love you more than anything!</i>

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:35.040
<i>Whether I'm asleep or awake, 
I keep thinking of you!</i>

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.630
<i>When I think that I might not be able 
to drink you again, it's so scary!</i>

00:13:40.390 --> 00:13:42.760
<i>Little things making you happy...</i>

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.920
<b>I ran out 
of booze!</b>

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.030
<i>or angry.</i>

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.230
<i>Moron!</i>

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:47.670
<i>Having daydreams about all kinds of things.</i>

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:51.320
<i>While traveling, wanting to drink 
so badly you can't stand it...</i>

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:51.320
<i>Don't go! Wait!</i>

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:52.940
<i>Take that!</i>

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:55.390
<i>And when it's not good enough, 
wanting to knee it...</i>

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:58.070
The instability of these emotions...

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:01.650
It is very close to a state of substance 
dependence or manic depression.

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:05.400
Bittersweet youth has changed in flash 
to something that seems super dangerous!

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:07.820
But... it's convincing.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:08.650
What?!

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:11.640
A pathological attachment 
to a single individual.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:14.160
Feelings of exaltation coupled 
with emotional instability.

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:17.500
If I were in the romantic phase, then...

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:21.350
from a neurocognitive perspective, 
I would truly be "lovesick."

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:24.920
<b>"Yukimura Dependence"</b>

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:24.610
A mental disorder that might be 
called "Yukimura Dependence"!

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:27.240
However, love isn't infinite.

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:29.550
According to research done 
by Fisher and others,

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:35.430
this violent romantic state lasts, 
at most, about three years.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:40.250
Both the palpitations of love and the 
maddening passion are eventually lost,

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:45.440
At that point, if the two 
maintain their relationship...

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:50.950
<b>Attachment</b>

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:50.950
<b>Attachment</b>

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:47.230
they reach the second stage...

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:50.950
the peaceful, stable attachment phase.

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:54.320
<i>My heart racing and fluttering...</i>

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:57.430
<i>that all disappeared long ago, but...</i>

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:01.570
<i>even so, I love this person.</i>

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:04.810
Couples who reach the attachment phase

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:09.560
feel a sense of security, comfort, 
and oneness with their partners.

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:11.850
The love hormone, oxytocin,

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:16.600
m 0 0 l 190 0 l 190 112 l 0 112

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:16.600
Oxytocin

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:14.360
and the hormone which stimulates 
paternal feelings, vasopressin,

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:16.600
m 0 0 l 190 0 l 190 112 l 0 112

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:16.600
Vasopressin

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:16.190
are released in large quantities.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:19.440
Feelings of security and comfort?

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:21.940
That's right.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:25.840
Fujiwara-san and Chris-san said 
they'd been dating for four years.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:29.600
Which means that they'd be 
in the attachment phase.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.490
I see. No wonder.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:40.020
Before, my heart used to race 
at how cool Chris was...

00:15:36.510 --> 00:15:38.370
Hello! I'm Chris!

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:46.750
<b>Yap</b>

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:46.750
<b>Yap</b>

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:45.550
But lately, I've thought he's 
cute, like a yapping Pomeranian.

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:48.290
I was thinking my heart hasn't raced much.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:51.250
That's how you see me?!

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:56.030
It can't be true. A Pomeranian?

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:58.300
As a man, I am a failure.

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:03.260
I'm half joking! Chris, you're the 
coolest person in the whole world.

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:08.000
And since they're in the attachment phase, 
they release a lot of oxytocin.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:13.270
That's why Chris-san and Fujiwara-san's 
oxytocin numbers are high.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:14.540
That's right.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:19.340
Oxytocin is primarily a hormone meant 
to stimulate breast milk production.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:22.260
When you touch someone you trust deeply,

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:24.320
putting you in a state of 
relaxation and happiness,

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:26.540
that's when it's produced the most.

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:28.530
After many years together,

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:30.970
you feel at peace with your sweetheart. 
And that lap-pillow...

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:33.960
is perfect for an oxytocin burst!

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.510
In contrast, the two of us...

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.170
even if we have fallen in love,

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:42.890
since we started in April, five months 
ago, we'd be in the romance stage.

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:45.930
So that's what it was!

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.990
Even when we make close contact, 
our hearts race and we get nervous.

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:53.020
We worry that we might reek of sweat.

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:56.320
It would be difficult to call 
that a state of relaxation.

00:16:56.980 --> 00:17:00.010
That's why not much oxytocin was produced!

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:01.210
If that's the case,

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:05.830
it makes sense that my and Himuro-senpai's 
oxytocin numbers were higher!

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:09.450
Since there wasn't the nervousness 
that happens between men and women,

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:12.090
we were able to make contact in a peaceful 
state much like the attachment phase.

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:16.140
A test of the oxytocin secretion levels of couples
with different lengths of romantic involvement in various circumstances
based on Helen Fisher's Three-year Romance Theory.

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:16.330
Following this theory, 
then everything is consistent!

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:18.590
There is only one conclusion!

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:22.640
True, our oxytocin levels are low.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:25.050
We were no match for you at all.

00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:28.890
However, that does not mean that 
we do not love each other!

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:39.850
My love for this woman will be 
proven through our research.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.400
I would ask you not to determine 
things based on suppositions!

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:48.150
<i>Didn't he basically just 
say that he loves her?</i>

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:51.420
<i>I was scared.</i>

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:55.650
<i>Would he let theories beat him?</i>

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:58.550
<i>Had we been wrong?</i>

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:01.190
<i>But...</i>

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:06.930
<i>in the end, he always demonstrates 
the answer he has for me.</i>

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:12.050
How frustrating.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:16.190
You're amazing, Yukimura-kun.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:19.440
Himuro...

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.680
What a perfect theory, Yukimura-kun.

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:29.030
It's a deeply interesting theory we can use 
in practical applications in our research.

00:18:29.030 --> 00:18:32.330
Yes. We were not wrong.

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:39.090
Hormones and the exact amounts of secretion 
in the brain comprise one element of love.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:44.680
And it isn't just oxytocin. 
Many different substances are involved!

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:49.200
If emotional stability plays 
a part in the romantic state,

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:52.590
then serotonin numbers may 
have some influence, as well.

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:52.590
<i>As I thought.</i>

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.480
<i>These two are best like this!</i>

00:18:57.060 --> 00:19:00.720
Those two are flaunting 
pretty well themselves.

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.000
That they are.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.260
<i>I see.</i>

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:09.250
<i>Whether right or wrong, they refused to 
accept that they were unworthy of love.</i>

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:13.710
<i>Instead, they dug up a new theory and 
showed that they were consistent with it.</i>

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:18.290
<i>So that's the shape 
your love takes, Yukimura-kun.</i>

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:20.480
<i>How very like a science-type.</i>

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:24.120
Thank you for everything.

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:27.570
If you ever need anything 
else measured, come back.

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:31.410
Work hard on your romance research.

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.780
Those two are a lovely couple, aren't they?

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:38.520
Though they were a pain.

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:41.540
But we gained important insight.

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:45.270
Bound to each other, a true couple...

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:47.820
Romantic love that blazes like fire...

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:50.350
Peaceful, gentle affectionate attachment...

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:54.180
Depending on the person, 
depending on the length of time, love...

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:56.000
takes many forms, doesn't it?

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:56.910
Yes.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:59.760
It seems there is need for further research.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:02.250
Yes, there is.

